  "name": "div-g-a-source-that-is-not-the-repository-expected",
  "note": "Divergence (g). The receiver expects the repository of genesis 0. A source whose current authority is 1, another repository's genesis, is asked for nothing: no commit is received, so read literally none fails and nothing is recorded. A source whose current authority is 2, which only k1 signed and so succeeds nothing, is asked for the valid c0: read literally it is recorded. The Rust looks at the source's current authority before anything it sent and refuses both. Asked for nothing by a receiver expecting the repository it is, a source is recorded as nothing under either reading.",
